From: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: ppe: invalidate stale routes

Retain each offloaded netfilter flow route generation and resolved
neighbour, then reject publication when either changes during the hardware
transaction. Register FIB and neighbour notifiers to disable installed PPE
rows before marking their netfilter flows for teardown.

Track the independently resolved underlay neighbour for IPIP6 tunnels and
apply the same validation around tunnel-backed flow installation. Keep
PPPoE and full-inline EIP paths exempt from an ordinary neighbour while
limiting PPE flowtable offload to the initial network namespace.

Expose route invalidation counters and state through debugfs so failed
hardware disables and stale-install rejections are visible during runtime
diagnosis.

Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-5.6-sol
Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
--- a/Documentation/networking/qualcomm-ppe-offload.rst
+++ b/Documentation/networking/qualcomm-ppe-offload.rst
@@ -184,11 +184,13 @@ per-flow hit counters feed the flowtable
 link-down port stop reporting activity so the flowtable expires and
 re-offloads them: hardware-forwarded packets never revalidate the
 route in software, and the hit counters count at ingress lookup
-whether or not egress delivery works. A route or neighbor that changes
-on the far side of a link that stays up is the remaining blind spot -
-such a flow keeps forwarding to the stale destination until its
-conntrack entry dies (the hardware flow aging engine, deliberately
-unused, could serve as a periodic revalidation net; see below).
+whether or not egress delivery works. Each direct route therefore retains
+its resolved neighbour and FIB generation. A final check brackets hardware
+publication, while FIB and neighbour notifiers disable stale rows and mark
+their netfilter flows for teardown. Tunnel encap rows retain and validate the
+separate underlay neighbour; PPPoE and full-inline EIP paths have no ordinary
+neighbour requirement. Offload is limited to the initial network namespace,
+whose FIB notifier is registered by the PPE instance.
 
 Datapath invariants worth knowing:
 
